# Game Performance Rules

## 1 · Scroll / RAF loop — no React state per frame

Never call `setState` / `useState` setter inside a `requestAnimationFrame` loop.
Drive scroll, position, and viewBox entirely through direct DOM writes.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — triggers React re-render every frame
const [worldOff, setWorldOff] = useState(0);
const loop = () => { setWorldOff(prev => prev + speed); raf = requestAnimationFrame(loop); };

// ✅ GOOD — direct attribute write, zero React overhead
const svgRef = useRef<SVGSVGElement>(null);
const loop = () => {
  svgRef.current?.setAttribute('viewBox', `${off} 0 1400 900`);
  raf = requestAnimationFrame(loop);
};
```

Only `facing`, `walking`, and `jumping` belong in React state (they change rarely and drive CSS classes).

## 2 · SVG layer CSS

Every parallax SVG layer must have these two CSS properties:

```tsx
style={{ willChange: 'transform', contain: 'layout style paint' }}
```

Non-critical decorative `<path>` elements (terrain fills, building shapes, etc.) should use `shapeRendering="optimizeSpeed"`.

## 3 · Tiling — render only the 3 nearest tiles

`ParallaxSvgLayer` already enforces 3 tiles. **Never** add a fourth tile or render outside the `[-1, 0, 1]` window.
Memoize tile render functions with `useCallback` (deps = tile index + period/theme only).
Wrap layer components in `React.memo` so they re-render only when their props change.

## 4 · NPCs — imperative DOM, throttled checks

NPC position and facing/walking must use the same direct-DOM pattern as the scroll loop:
- `divRef.current.style.left = …` for position
- `characterRef.current?.setFacing(…)` / `setWalking(…)` via `useImperativeHandle`

Proximity and dance-state checks run **every 4 frames** (`frameCount % 4 === 0`), not every frame.

## 5 · YouTube iframes

```tsx
// Always add loading="lazy"
<iframe loading="lazy" src={embedSrc} … />

// Use youtube-nocookie.com + suppress chrome
function embedSrc(id: string) {
  return `https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/${id}?autoplay=1&mute=1&rel=0&modestbranding=1&controls=0&iv_load_policy=3&loop=1&playlist=${id}`;
}
```

Iframe lifecycle is controlled by the `live` prop from `isVenueInView` — do **not** add a second `IntersectionObserver` inside an SVG `foreignObject` (it won't fire reliably).

## 6 · SVG path strings — pre-compute at module load

Paths whose coordinates are constants must be pre-computed **outside** the component.
Template literals with constant variables recompute on every render — extract them.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — recomputed on every render
const PEAK_X = 1855, PEAK_Y = 268;
<path d={`M1235,578 Q1500,508 ${PEAK_X},${PEAK_Y} Z`} />

// ✅ GOOD — static string, zero allocation per render
const SNOW_PATH = 'M1235,578 Q1500,508 1855,268 Z';
<path d={SNOW_PATH} />
```

Avoid `Array.from(…).map(…)` inside JSX for window grids, mullion lines, pier geometry, etc.
Replace with a **single pre-computed path string** or a module-level static array.
